X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","cwe":["CWE-119","CWE-121"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-94051","title":"A vulnerability was found in 0717376 cowork_bench up to d943e75bc0fc8e3b27141979300cd8cbcd1e890d.","desc":"A vulnerability was found in 0717376 cowork_bench up to d943e75bc0fc8e3b27141979300cd8cbcd1e890d. Affected by this vulnerability is the function ControlFlowNode of the file local_servers/pdf-tools-mcp/pdf_tools_mcp/server.py of the component pdf-tools-mcp. Performing a manipulation of the argument pdf_file_path results in server-side request forgery. It is possible to initiate the attack remotely. The exploit has been made public and could be used. This product is using a rolling release to provide continious delivery. Therefore, no version details for affected nor updated releases are available. The project was informed of the problem early through an issue report but has not responded yet.","score":2.1,"sev":"low","published":"2026-09-20T21:16:55.597Z","modified":"2026-09-21T17:19:19.273Z","window_date":"2026-09-20","activity_at":"2026-09-20T21:31:34Z","date_basis":"GitHub advisory publication","affected":[],"refs":[{"label":"NVD record","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-94051","source":"NVD"},{"label":"CVE Program record","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-94051","source":"CVE Program"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/0717376/cowork_bench/","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/0717376/cowork_bench/issues/1","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/Xh1Xxhg/public_exp/issues/7","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-94051","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/submit/949604","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/vuln/407980","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/vuln/407980/cti","source":"NVD"},{"label":"GitHub security advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6j48-ggfg-8xw2","source":"GitHub"},{"label":"Advisory reference","url":"https://github.com/0717376/cowork_bench","source":"GitHub"}],"related_cves":[],"advisories":[{"label":"GitHub Security Advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6j48-ggfg-8xw2"}],"sources":["NVD","GitHub Advisory Database"],"kev":null,"primary_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-94051","cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","cwe":["CWE-918"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-94050","title":"A vulnerability has been found in D-Link DIR-X1860Z up to 1.0.2.220120.165402.","desc":"A vulnerability has been found in D-Link DIR-X1860Z up to 1.0.2.220120.165402. Affected is the function routerd.wificfg_get/routerd.get_rand_key of the component ubus JSON-RPC interface. Such manipulation leads to information disclosure. The attack must be carried out from within the local network. Upgrading to version 1.0.7.260821.161908 is able to address this issue. It is suggested to upgrade the affected component. This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer.","score":5.3,"sev":"medium","published":"2026-09-20T21:16:55.380Z","modified":"2026-09-24T13:17:17.090Z","window_date":"2026-09-20","activity_at":"2026-09-20T21:31:34Z","date_basis":"GitHub advisory publication","affected":[],"refs":[{"label":"NVD record","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-94050","source":"NVD"},{"label":"CVE Program record","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-94050","source":"CVE Program"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://support.dlink.com/resource/SECURITY_ADVISEMENTS/DIR-X1860Z/DIR-X1860Z_REVA_FIRMWARE_V1.0.7.260821.161908_HOTFIX.zip","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://supportannouncement.us.dlink.com/security/publication.aspx?name=SAP10513","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/cv